**Site Report – Station Egwi, Etche LGA**

The VES interpretation at Station Egwi reveals a five-layer subsurface sequence with resistivity increasing progressively with depth. Layer 1 (0–0.545 m) has a resistivity of 295.88 Ω·m, underlain by Layer 2 (798.6 Ω·m, to 4.14 m), Layer 3 (864.62 Ω·m, to 6.29 m), Layer 4 (1810.2 Ω·m, to 37.25 m), and a resistive basal Layer 5 (5634.2 Ω·m, unbounded). This monotonic increase in resistivity with depth is consistent across all three-layer groupings (1-2-3, 2-3-4, 3-4-5), each satisfying r1 < r2 < r3, yielding an AAA sequence, correctly simplified to a single A-type curve. The classification on file (A-type) is consistent with the layer resistivity values and requires no revision. This profile likely reflects increasing compaction or lithological change with depth, useful for borehole placement planning.

